{
  "step_1": "The decision reason considers whether either lottery contains a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome that occurs with 100% probability). In Lottery A, the outcomes are -3000 Euros with 0.2% probability and 0 Euros with 99.8% probability. In Lottery B, the outcomes are -6000 Euros with 0.1% probability and 0 Euros with 99.9% probability. Neither lottery has a sure outcome (100% probability), as both involve non-zero probabilities for losing and for gaining nothing. Therefore, the condition for the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) is not satisfied in either lottery. The reason would be indifferent or not applicable because no lottery offers a sure outcome.",
